course: dictionary
lesson: 10212
title: Tit: a small bird, and tit for tat
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Some great tits sing higher to be heard over the traffic.» Birds sing, and great tits are a kind of bird, so tit here means a small, lively bird.
explain: Look at «tit for tat» carefully. Tit here is not a bird. It is part of a phrase, and the phrase has its own meaning. Tit for tat means doing something bad back to someone because they did it to you. You cannot get that meaning from each word alone.
explain: Use the check: swap your meaning into the sentence. «Blue tits time their chicks to hatch when caterpillars are most common.» Put in "small bird" and it makes sense. Always read the clues around a word before you decide what it means.
fact: A tit is a small, lively bird, and it is a noun.
fact: Blue tits and great tits are common in gardens in the UK and Europe.
fact: Blue tits eat caterpillars and seeds, and they feed their chicks caterpillars.
fact: «Tit for tat» means doing something bad back to someone because they did it to you.
fact: Phrases like «blue tit» and «great tit» are names of birds.
exercise: «Blue tits time their chicks to hatch when caterpillars are most common.» In this sentence, what is a tit? | A type of caterpillar | A nest in the hedge | *A small, lively bird | A kind of tree
exercise: «Tit for tat» means what? | Hiding in a tree until dark | *Doing something bad back to someone because they did it to you | Singing very loudly at night | Sharing your lunch with a friend
exercise: Copy the word for a bird from «City life changes animals too: robins sing under streetlamps at night.» | *robins | animals | night | streetlamps
test: «A pair of blue tits can bring around 10 000 caterpillars to one brood.» What do blue tits bring to their brood? | *Caterpillars | Worms | Seeds | Berries
test: Which phrase means doing something bad back to someone because they did it to you? | *Tit for tat | Blue tit | Great tit | Long-tailed tit
exam: «A pair of blue tits can bring around 10 000 caterpillars to one brood.» In this sentence, what does tit mean? | A nest in a tree | *A small, lively bird | A kind of seed | A type of caterpillar
